I live in Flagstaff.  Please explain to me how the final map accomplishes anything beyond your first of six goals!
1. Equal population;
2. Compactness and contiguousness;
3. Compliance with the U.S. Constitution and the Voting Rights Act;
4. Respect for communities of interest;
5. Incorporation of visible geographic features, including city, town and county boundaries, as well as undivided census tracts; and
6. Creation of competitive districts where there is no significant detriment to other goals.

The IRC has failed at even reaching the second goal.  You have divided flagstaff in a ridiculous way and have stuck half the city in a district that reaches almost to Tucson and the other half reaches to Colorado and Utah!

Do you really want us to be forced to legally challenge this in court and for the whole process to be destroyed?

Mark Haughwout
928-607-4034
